THIRD-PARTY TEXTS:

These files quote prayers, liturgical formulas, Scripture and Catechism passages
that holystack.dev does not own and cannot sub-license. They are included as
quotations for devotional use, and all rights remain with their respective
holders. Nothing in this license grants any right over them.

This includes, but is not limited to:
- Vernacular translations of the Our Father, Hail Mary, Glory Be, the Apostles'
  Creed, the Act of Contrition, the Salve Regina and the Rosary mysteries, whose
  approved translations belong to the relevant episcopal conferences and
  liturgical commissions (ICEL, CEI, AELF, CBCK, KWI, CCBI, CNBB and others).
- The formula of absolution and other texts of the Order of Penance (ICEL and
  the corresponding vernacular commissions).
- Scripture quotations, which belong to the copyright holders of the translation
  quoted in each language.
- Excerpts from and citations of the Catechism of the Catholic Church
  (© Libreria Editrice Vaticana).

If you hold rights in any text quoted here and want it attributed differently or
removed, please open an issue.

---

RATIONALE:

This content license is chosen to protect the integrity of Catholic spiritual
content. The examination of conscience questions, prayers, and guides must remain
accurate to Catholic teaching. The NoDerivatives clause ensures that modified
versions with potentially incorrect spiritual content cannot be distributed.

Translations to other languages are welcome but must be submitted as Pull Requests
to the main repository where they can be reviewed for accuracy before inclusion.

